{
 "_doc": "Forest set pieces, round 4 (ADR-0053): Shiloh Chapel, a pioneer timber chapel in a forest clearing half taken back by the woods: its bell-cote fallen into the long grass, ivy in through the lancets, a lych gate in a tumbled churchyard wall, leaning stones, the Teague family plot in its iron railing, an open grave and graves the Bloom has broken. Below: the undercroft where the pastor nursed the sick (level -1, under the nave and the vestry) and the Teague vault dug into the bank (a kit room under the w4_chapel_mausoleum_front shell, a switchback stair down to level -1 and on to the buried vault on level -2: its niche hall, the inner vault and the pastor's passage back up into the undercroft). Route: through the lych gate (cans) -> the front doors boarded by the Cordon -> round the east side past the open grave (jaws in the grass) -> in by a smashed window over a crate -> the nave (the vigil in the pews wakes) -> the narthex ladder up to the choir loft (loose boards; the register) -> down by the gap in the loft rail -> through the broken floor into the undercroft (the sick wake) -> up the ladder into the vestry (barricaded from inside: the diary and the vault key) -> out by the vestry's bolted back door -> the Teague plot (a letter on a grave) -> the vault's chained iron door (the key) -> down the switchback -> the niche hall (the dead in the walls wake) -> the inner vault (the pastor, guardian; the silver and the reliquary) -> the bolted passage back up into the undercroft -> the vestry ladder and out. Props: props/wild4_chapel.json.",
